# Command copyq

## What does this command do:

CLI interface to the CopyQ clipboard manager daemon — inspect history, read/write entries, control the GUI, and automate via scripting

## Installed from

For Mac install using: DMG from https://github.com/hluk/CopyQ/releases/latest
(Do NOT use `brew install --cask copyq` — deprecated, unsigned, crashes on macOS 26+)
See desktop-apps-configuration-and-runbooks/CopyQ/RUNBOOK.md for full install procedure.

## Command path

For Mac run: /Applications/CopyQ.app/Contents/MacOS/copyq

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://hluk.github.io/CopyQ/

## Command options

# --- History inspection ---

# Count items in history
copyq count

# Print most recent item (index 0 = newest)
copyq read 0

# Print items at specific rows
copyq read 0 1 2

# Print last 10 items with index numbers
for i in $(seq 0 9); do echo "[$i] $(copyq read $i | head -c 100)"; done

# Print current clipboard contents
copyq clipboard

# --- Writing / modifying history ---

# Set clipboard to text
copyq copy "some text"

# Add text to history without changing the live clipboard
copyq add "some text"

# Insert text at a specific row
copyq insert 0 "text"

# Delete item at row 0 (most recent)
copyq remove 0

# Copy item at row N to the live clipboard
copyq select 3

# --- Navigation ---

# Copy next item from history to clipboard
copyq next

# Copy previous item from history to clipboard
copyq previous

# --- Window control ---

# Show main CopyQ window
copyq show

# Hide main window
copyq hide

# Toggle main window visibility
copyq toggle

# Open context menu (tray)
copyq menu

# --- Daemon control ---

# Pause clipboard monitoring
copyq disable

# Resume clipboard monitoring
copyq enable

# Shut down the daemon
copyq exit

# --- Tabs ---

# List all tab names
copyq tab

# Run command on a named tab
copyq tab "MyTab" count

# Remove a tab
copyq removetab "MyTab"

# Rename a tab
copyq renametab "OldName" "NewName"

# Export/import tab history
copyq exporttab /tmp/clipboard-backup.cpq
copyq importtab /tmp/clipboard-backup.cpq

# --- Config ---

# List all config options
copyq config

# Get a single option
copyq config maxitems

# Set max history size (default 200)
copyq config maxitems 500

# --- Scripting ---

# Evaluate JavaScript in the CopyQ scripting engine
copyq eval 'print(size())'
copyq eval 'popup("Title", "Message")'

# Search history for a string
copyq eval 'for(var i=0;i<size();i++) if(str(read(i)).match(/searchterm/)) print("["+i+"] "+str(read(i)).slice(0,80)+"\n")'

# --- Verify CopyQ is alive and capturing ---
TEST="verify-$(date +%s)"; printf '%s' "$TEST" | pbcopy; sleep 1; [ "$(copyq read 0)" = "$TEST" ] && echo OK || echo FAIL
